\f1\b \cf0 5. Summation.
\f0\b0  At a current price of $110 per barrel (unverified), the barrels in use cost $660.0M, plus the $498.2M cumulative loss, for a total of $1,158.2M, or 
\f1\b $193.04 per barrel in use
\f0\b0 . Stacking all four years onto one barrel gives $424.50 on a crude basis and about $663 on a fully refined basis, but that charges multi-year losses to a single barrel.\

